  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **On and On**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n- **Midnight Moonlight**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Old Mexico**: back after 70 archived shows (449 days) [2]\n- **Beauty of Dreams**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Circles**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2020-09-19.oktava.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 23 songs; 132 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was two sets with no encore, billed as the Meet Me at the Drive-In Tour [1]\n- Exposition Gardens is where the Heart of Illinois Fair is held [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2020-09-19.oktava.flac16**: taped by Michael Frasca; transferred by Michael Frasca; source: Audience, left of soundboard, 150 feet from stage, MJE-modified Oktava MK-012 cardioids in an A-B pattern with 10cm of spread-> Tascam DR-40-> wav @44.1K-> SD… [1]. Also: Recorded with Oktava microphones from the 4th row of the Silver Section, well left of the soundboard [1]",
